  Reel_script says 'திருச்சி மாநகரில்' (in Trichy city) for the seizures, which matches the article; no issue there. However, the reel_script and slides say the officers 'பி. முருகானந்தம் தலைமையிலான' conducted inspections, which matches. The main problem: the reel_script and slides say the seized air horns were 'விதிமீறிய' and the caption says 'வாகனங்களில் சட்டவிதிகளை மீறி வைக்கப்பட்டிருந்த', which is acceptable. Real issue: the caption's first paragraph says the air horns were seized and 'போக்குவரத்துத் துறையினர் ரூ. 1 லட்சம் அபராதம் விதித்தனர்' – consistent. The slide 'எத்தனை வாகனங்கள்?' line reads '7 தனியார் பேருந்துகள், ஒரு கல்லூரி வாகனம், ஒரு மில்' and omits the lorry, which is a missing fact, but the slide line is truncated rather than wrong.
  Slide 2 line 1 says '50க்கும் மேற்பட்ட தனியார் பேருந்துகள், கல்லூரி' which wrongly attributes the 50+ inspected vehicles only to private buses and college vehicles, omitting lorries, which the article says were also inspected (50+ private buses, college vehicles, lorries).
  The reel_script states the penalty was 'மொத்தம் ரூ. 1 லட்சம்' and per vehicle Rs 10,000 each; the article says Rs 10,000 per vehicle for the 10 vehicles, which matches the total, so no error there.
  The reel_script omits the lorry from the list of vehicles where horns were seized, which is an important detail of the article (the full breakdown of seized vehicles is incomplete in the reel_script, which lists only 'அதிக ஒலி எழுப்பும் காற்று ஒலிப்பான்கள்' without the vehicle breakdown).
